      "id": "ML-C66-paddy",
      "sequence": 2190,
      "title": "നെല്ല് (nellŭ) — unhusked rice, rice still in the husk",
      "headword": "നെല്ല്",
      "romanization": "nellŭ",
      "gloss": "unhusked rice, rice still in the husk",
      "script": "malayalam",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:49d2629be240bd3c",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new run of words: what did maryāda mean, and what did viśvāsaṁ mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: നെല്ല്",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "നെല്ല് (nellŭ) — \"unhusked rice, rice still in the husk\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Native Dravidian, matching Tamil nel, and it completes a set you have been collecting a piece at a time. നെല്ല് (nellŭ) is the grain in the husk and in the field; ari is the same grain husked; cōṟŭ is it cooked."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three words for one plant is what a language does when the plant is the year's whole work. The flooded field you already know by name, vayal, is where the first of the three lives."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It sounds like ellŭ, the bone-word, with an n set in front. The two have nothing to do with one another, and the front of the word is again where the ear earns its keep."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "നെല്ല് (nellŭ) is native Dravidian, one word with Tamil nel and Kannada nel (DEDR 3753)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The first of five words from the paddy."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
